Provides: phone-mcp-server, python3-phone-mcp
Replaces: phone-mcp-server (<< 0.3.7-2~), python3-phone-mcp (<< 0.3.6-2~)
Breaks: phone-mcp-server (<< 0.3.7-2~), python3-phone-mcp (<< 0.3.6-2~)
Description: MCP plugin for controlling Android phones via ADB
 Phone MCP is a Model Context Protocol plugin that lets an AI assistant
 control an Android phone through the Android Debug Bridge (ADB).
 .
 It exposes tools for calls, messaging, contacts, media, app management,
 UI interaction, and screen analysis, allowing an MCP-aware assistant to
 automate and inspect a connected Android device.

Package: mcprack-mcp-server-adb
Architecture: all
Depends:
 ${misc:Depends},
 mcprack (>= 1.5.1),
 mcp-server-adb (= ${binary:Version}),
Provides: mcprack-mcp-server-phone
Replaces: mcprack-mcp-server-phone (<< 0.3.7-2~)
Breaks: mcprack-mcp-server-phone (<< 0.3.7-2~)
Description: Registers ADB Phone MCP server into mcprack catalog
 Companion package for mcp-server-adb. Installing it registers the
 phone-mcp binary as an available MCP server in the local mcprack
 instance; removing it unregisters it again.
